===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=tall|:inh|enm:heigh|tree=1}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kewk-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|high}}, {{m|enm|heigh}}, {{m|enm|heih}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hēah|t=high, tall, lofty, high-class, exalted, sublime, illustrious, important, proud, haughty, deep, right}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hauh|t=high}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hauhaz|t=high}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kewk-|t=to bend; crooked}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|heich|t=high}}, {{cog|yol|heegh}}, {{m|yol|heigh}}, {{m|yol|heighe}}, {{m|yol|hia}}, {{m|yol|hie|t=high}}, {{cog|frr|hoog}}, {{m|frr|huuch|t=high}}, {{cog|stq|hooch}}, {{m|stq|hoog|t=high}}, {{cog|fy|heech|t=high}}, {{cog|gsw|hooch|t=high}}, {{cog|gmw-cfr|huh|t=high}}, {{cog|cim|hoach}}, {{m|cim|hòach|t=high}}, {{cog|nl|hoog|t=high}}, {{cog|de|hoch|t=high}}, {{cog|nds-de|hooch|t=high}}, {{cog|li|hoeg|t=high}}, {{cog|lb|héich|t=high}}, {{cog|mhn|heach|t=high}}, {{cog|wym|huch|t=high}}, {{cog|yi|הויך|t=high}}, {{cog|da|høj|t=high}}, {{cog|fo|háur}}, {{m|fo|høgur|t=high}}, {{cog|gmq-gut|haugar|t=high}}, {{cog|is|hár|t=high}}, {{cog|nb|høg}}, {{m|nb|høy|t=high}}, {{cog|nn|høg}}, {{m|nn|håg}}, {{m|nn|hå|t=high}}, {{cog|sv|hög|t=high}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌿𐌷𐍃|t=high}}, {{cog|xvn|*oas|t=high}}, {{cog|fro|haut|t=high}} (from {{cog|goh|hoh|t=high}}); also with {{cog|grc|Καύκᾰσος|t=Caucasus}}, {{cog|lv|koks|t=tree}}, {{cog|lt|kúoka|t=stick with thick end, pounder, pestle}}, {{cog|bg|ку́ка|t=hook}}, {{cog|sq|çukë|t=peak, summit, top}}.
