#: {{ux|en|'''high''' voltage &nbsp; '''high''' prices &nbsp; '''high''' winds &nbsp; a '''high''' number}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|1|passage=Can heavenly minds such '''high''' resentment show?}}
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=w:Tom Whitlock|composer=w:Giorgio Moroder|authorlabel=no|title={{w|Danger Zone (song)|Danger Zone}}|album={{w|Top Gun (soundtrack)|Top Gun}}|date=24 April 1986|artist=w:Kenny Loggins|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yK0P1Bk8Cx4|text=You'll never say hello to you<br>Until you get it on the red line overload<br>You'll never know what you can do<br>Until you get it up as '''high''' as you can go}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Tracy Martin|title=How To Diagnose and Repair Automotive Electrical Systems|url=https://www.worldcat.org/title/how-to-diagnose-and-repair-automotive-electrical-systems/oclc/475398375|page=16|text=Ignition voltage needs to be high enough to overcome the '''high''' resistance created by the air gap.}}
#* {{quote-journal| 1=en| year=2013| month=July-August| author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/fenella-saunders Fenella Saunders]| magazine=w:American Scientist| title=Tiny Lenses See the Big Picture| url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/tiny-lenses-see-the-big-picture| passage=The single-imaging optic of the mammalian eye offers some distinct visual advantages. Such lenses can take in photons from a wide range of angles, increasing light sensitivity. They also have '''high''' spatial resolution, resolving incoming images in minute detail.| archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130907101516/http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/tiny-lenses-see-the-big-picture| archivedate=7 September 2013}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Richard H. Pildes|title=The three words that can avert an election nightmare|url=https://www.cnn.com/2020/09/14/opinions/election-2020-vote-by-mail-absentee-pildes|date=2020-09-14|passage=Studies also show that absentee ballots cast by voters who are younger or from racial and ethnic minority groups are rejected at '''higher''' rates than other absentee ballots.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260616040748/https://www.cnn.com/2020/09/14/opinions/election-2020-vote-by-mail-absentee-pildes|archivedate=16 June 2026}}
## {{sid|en|greater concentration}} Having a large or comparatively larger [[concentration]] of (a [[substance]], {{n-g|which is often but not always linked by "{{m|en|in}}" when predicative}}).
##: {{ux|en|Carrots are '''high''' in [[vitamin A]]. &nbsp; made from a '''high'''-copper alloy}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1907|title=The American Exporter|volume=60|page=101
|passage=Anyone can determine for himself whether certain wire is '''high''' carbon or not. Heat a piece of the wire red hot and while red plunge into water till cold.}}
# {{sid|en|pitch}} {{lb|en|acoustics}} {{cap|acute}} or [[shrill]] in [[pitch]], due to being of greater [[frequency]], i.e. produced by more [[rapid]] vibrations (wave [[oscillation]]s).
#: {{ux|en|The note was too '''high''' for her to sing.}}
# {{sid|en|phonetics}} {{lb|en|phonetics}} Made with some part of the tongue positioned high in the mouth, relatively close to the palate.
# {{sid|en|playing cards}} {{lb|en|card games}} Greater in value than other cards, [[denomination]]s, suits, etc.
## {{sid|en|poker}} {{lb|en|poker}} Having the highest [[rank]] in a [[straight]], [[flush]] or [[straight flush]].
##: {{ux|en|I have KT742 of the same suit. In other words, a K-'''high''' flush.}}
##: {{ux|en|9-'''high''' straight <nowiki>=</nowiki> 98765 unsuited}}
##: {{ux|en|Royal Flush <nowiki>=</nowiki> AKQJT suited <nowiki>=</nowiki> A-'''high''' straight flush}}
## {{sid|en|able to take trick}} {{lb|en|of a card or hand}} Winning; able to take a [[trick]], win a round, etc.
##: {{ux|en|North's hand was '''high'''. East was in trouble.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1894|journal=Harper's Magazine|volume=88|page=910
|passage=Cutler pushed forward the two necessary white chips. No one's hand was '''high''', and Loomis made a slight winning.}}
# {{sid|en|strongly scented meat}} {{lb|en|of meat|especially venison}} Strong-scented; slightly tainted/spoiled; beginning to decompose.
#: {{ux|en|Epicures do not cook game before it is '''high'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The tailor liked his meat '''high'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=Stephen King|title=Needful Things|passage=What he did know was this: something about the situation smelled wrong. Something about it smelled as '''high''' as dead fish that have spent three days in the hot sun.}}
# {{sid|en|nautical}} {{lb|en|nautical|of a|sailing ship}} Near, in its direction of travel, to the (direction of the) [[wind]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1784|author=William Falconer|title=An Universal Dictionary of the Marine: Or, A Copious Explanation|passage=NO NEARER! (''arrive!'' Fr.) the command given by the pilot of quarter-master, to the helmsman, to steer the ship no '''higher''' to the direction of the wind than the sails will operate to advance the ship in her course.}}
# {{sid|en|team sports}} {{lb|en|sports such as|_|soccer}} Positioned up the field, towards the opposing team's goal.
#: {{ux|en|Our defensive line is too '''high'''.}}

